            <profile id="cc7d-d492-eaa3-611f" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword, light armour, shield. May be mounted on a horse (+8 pts). May have javelins (+2 pts), throwing spear or thrusting spear (+2 pts). May wear heavy armour (+1 pt). If no other Army General is taken, the army may be led by a Christian Captain (+25 pts; not in the Caliphate of Cordoba). You may not have both a Christian Captain and Berber Shaykh in the same army. 0-1. Taifa Kings and Later Taifas: may ride a warhorse (+16 pts). Later Taifas: may exchange thrusting or throwing spear for lance (+4 pts) and have horse barding (+2 pts); characters may have a lance (+6 pts). (El Cid p.40)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="24f1-f4f1-8bf7-ae3d" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
