            <profile id="d764-e8db-8623-6ce1" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword. May have light armour (+3 pts), shield (+2 pts), javelins (+1 pt), throwing spear (+2 pts). May be mounted on a horse (+8 pts). The Qadi can lead a single formed unit (not skirmishers) which may re-roll failed Rally attempts while the Qadi is alive and leading. 0-1. Later Taifas: if no other Army General is chosen, the Qadi may be made Army General for +50 pts (units he leads may also re-roll failed Panic tests; the Qadi-General loses the Rally re-roll). Taifa Kings and Later Taifas: may ride a warhorse (+16 pts). Later Taifas: may wear heavy armour (no lance). (El Cid p.40)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="844b-abe5-ebff-37ce" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
