            </profile>
            <profile id="b96e-87f4-c746-ca38" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapons, horse and latch (light crossbow). May have shields (+1 pt) and/or light armour (+2 pts). Light Cavalry. Feigned Flight. Andalusian Horsemen. The light crossbow has a range of 24", Strength 3 and a -1 save modifier; units that move in the Movement phase cannot fire that turn. 0-1 unit. Later Taifas only. (El Cid p.42)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="2a09-7c6b-34bf-76a0" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
