  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="375e-6ccc-9f4a-53a3" name="Al-Andalus (El Cid) - List Notes" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false">
      <description>AL-ANDALUS ARMY LIST (El Cid, pp.35-42): the Caliphate of Cordoba (c.912-1008), the Taifa Kings (c.1008-1110) and the Later Taifas and Nasrid Granada (c.1110-1250). Percentages are by points. Special rules p.37 (Andalusian Horsemen).
Not enforced: "at least half the number of cavalry models selected must be Andalusian Jinetes" (a cross-unit figure percentage), and up to half the units of Andalusian Jinetes may have bows. The printed Later Taifas rule gives heavy armour for characters at +3 pts, the same as light armour; heavy armour is therefore entered at no extra charge over light armour.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Caliphate]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: Caliphate: at least 50%
  Uncommon Troops: Caliphate: up to 33%
  The Caliphate of Cordoba, c.912-1008 AD (p.37). Characters up to 25% (Caliph, Amir, Berber Shaykh, Christian Captain, Alferez, Cantador, Qadi; the Army General may be a Caliph, Amir or Berber Shaykh, but not a Christian Captain). Common Troops at least 50%: Andalusian Jinetes, Noble Cavalry, Spearmen, Archers, Skirmishers, Mercenary Spearmen and Archers. Uncommon Troops up to 33%: Mercenary Jinetes and Mercenary Caballeros. At least half the number of cavalry models selected must be Andalusian Jinetes.
[Taifa Kings]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: Taifa Kings: at least 33%
  Uncommon Troops: Taifa Kings: up to 50%
  The Taifa Kings, c.1008-1110 AD (p.38). Characters up to 25% (Amir, Berber Shaykh, Christian Captain, Alferez, Cantador, Qadi; the Army General may be an Amir, Berber Shaykh or Christian Captain). Characters may ride warhorses (+16 pts). Common Troops at least 33%: Andalusian Jinetes, Noble Cavalry, Spearmen, Archers, Skirmishers. Uncommon Troops up to 50%: Andalusian Crossbowmen (0-1 unit only), Mercenary Spearmen, Archers, Jinetes, Crossbowmen and Knights. At least half the number of cavalry models selected must be Andalusian Jinetes.
[Later Taifas]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: Later Taifas: at least 33%
  Uncommon Troops: Later Taifas: up to 50%
  Survivors and Renegades - the Later Taifas and Nasrid Granada, c.1110-1250 AD (pp.38-39). Characters up to 25% (Amir, Berber Shaykh, Christian Captain, Alferez, Cantador, Qadi; the Army General may be an Amir, Berber Shaykh, Christian Captain or a Qadi). Characters may ride warhorses (+16 pts) and wear heavy armour (+3 pts); any character except the Alferez or Qadi may have a lance (+6 pts). Andalusian Jinetes and Mercenary Jinetes may take light armour (+2 pts per model). Christian Captains and Mercenary Knights may exchange spears for lances (+4 pts per model) and have horse barding (+2 pts). If no other Army General is chosen the Qadi may be made Army General (+50 pts). Common Troops at least 33%: Andalusian Jinetes, Noble Cavalry, Knights, Spearmen, Archers, Skirmishers, Crossbowmen, Mounted Crossbowmen. Uncommon Troops up to 50%: Mercenary Spearmen, Archers, Jinetes, Crossbowmen and Knights. At least half the number of cavalry models selected must be Andalusian Jinetes.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
